WEBVTT

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.880
Oh, goodness, me.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:52.760
Excellent timing, Rika.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.640
I'll be right there!
Just one moment, please!

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:01.770
I'm here to pick you up!

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:05.650
I'm all ready to go.

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:09.020
Come, now! Tonight is Watanagashi!

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:15.030
Is your house still dirty?
I can help clean up a bit if you want!

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:17.740
That won't be necessary.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:22.250
It's only in a bit
of disarray, that's all.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:53.000
HIGURASHI: WHEN THEY CRY SOTSU

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:58.380
Do forgive me for the delay, everyone!

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.840
Satoko-<i>chan</i>!

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:04.140
The coach told me you were supposed
to stop by the clinic for a check-up,

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.220
but you said no.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.640
That's right, I'm fit as a fiddle!

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:12.730
I get it! You were scared to spend
the night there by yourself, huh?

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:17.650
After all, Satoko can't fall asleep
without me in bed with her.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:21.160
What's that supposed to imply? What?!

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.910
Well, you see--

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:24.330
Hold it right there!

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:27.790
I was going to hear you out, but my,
what kind of person do you take me for?

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:35.500
I thought we'd never get these happy,
fun times back...

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:39.510
Yeah, but we got 'em back.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:40.880
Together.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.050
Yeah.

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:44.800
Okay! We've got Kei-<i>chan</i>
and Shion with us this year,

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:47.890
so it's time for the Watanagashi
Six-Demon Battle Royale!

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:51.270
My, already? I won't hold back, you know!

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:54.360
No idea what that is,
but I'm down for a battle!

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:58.030
Okay, rules for today are simple:
whoever has the most fun, wins!

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.150
That sound good?

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:00.820
Yeah!

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:10.080
Hanyuu...

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:14.630
Even if you can't be by my side anymore...

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:18.760
Even if you can't see
these happy moments...

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:23.590
I'll still tell you, again and again.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:28.350
Hey, Satoko-<i>chan</i>!

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:25.890
Just look at this.

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:28.350
We managed to win.

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:32.600
We've changed our
tragic future once again.

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:44.450
You don't need to worry anymore, Hanyuu.

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:48.990
We've escaped this dead end.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.790
We can create our own miracles...

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:56.250
...and cut ourselves free of fate!

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:09.570
Satoko?

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:11.450
It's just getting started...

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:26.470
Satoko, you sly devil.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:30.100
What'd you want to talk to me up here for?

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:32.010
Rika told me everything.

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:35.930
About how you hard you worked
to help me, everything.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:39.690
It was no big deal.
We're friends, aren't we?

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:44.190
I'm really thankful
for all you've done for me.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:48.450
I'm sorry, but I have one
more favor to ask of you.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:51.280
Would it be all right...

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:55.790
...if I called you "Nii-Nii"?

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:57.620
Huh? But isn't that...

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:59.670
You don't like the nickname "Nii-Nii"?

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:02.460
N-No, it's fine, I just...

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.750
Then it's settled!

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:05.880
Nii-Nii!

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:08.840
Nii-Nii!

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:14.760
Y-Yeah!

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:19.900
Also, there's something
I'd like to give you.

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:23.940
It was something
very important to my Nii-Nii.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:26.820
But now that <i>you're</i>
my Nii-Nii, Keiichi-<i>san</i>,

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:29.950
I want <i>you </i>to have it.

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:32.120
If you really feel that way, then sure.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:36.620
I'm embarrassed for anyone
to know about this,

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:38.830
so let's go before they know we're gone!

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:08.820
Dammit!

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:12.660
Why does it have to be so damn itchy?!

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:15.160
Itchy, itchy, itchy!

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:27.500
What's this? You again, Maebara-<i>san</i>?

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:32.720
Come on now, don't be a stranger!

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:36.100
After all, this is
your house too, Nii-Nii!

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:44.100
Hey, Satoko, your uncle
got arrested, right?

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:48.480
That's right. We're the only ones
here right now.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:50.900
It's just you and me.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:53.820
So what was that thing
you wanted to give me?

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:56.240
Wait right here, okay?

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:57.530
Okay.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:09.340
Let's see, where's the switch...

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:24.730
Rika...

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:30.610
This is the end of your little miracle.

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:35.320
It's time, now...

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:41.330
...for your despair!

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:27.710
The rest I leave to you, Ooishi-<i>san</i>.

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:39.390
No!

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:43.100
Hojo-<i>san</i>!

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:50.610
What happened?! Whose blood is that?!

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:55.690
You were just with
Maebara-<i>san</i>, weren't you?

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:58.950
Where is he? And where is Teppei-<i>san</i>?!

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:04.830
This is pointless!

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:41.320
G-Good god...

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.620
Keiichi-<i>san </i>did it.

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:46.200
Keiichi-<i>san </i>said it was the curse.

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:48.790
What about the curse?!

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:53.460
Did he attack Teppei because
he's an enemy of the village?!

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:56.590
If you're trying to protect him,
then you're <i>just </i>as guilty!

00:12:56.590 --> 00:13:00.010
Ugh, I'm so damn itchy!

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:03.180
He came to me
when I was watching Rika's dance.

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:04.600
What?

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:09.770
Keiichi-<i>san </i>grabbed my hand
and took me away from the shrine.

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:13.730
He said we really needed
to go to my house and talk.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:16.860
Keiichi Maebara invited himself over?

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:20.400
To the home where
their enemy, Teppei, lived?

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:24.200
No, no, someone must have
told him to do it!

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:27.830
Someone in the village.
The person behind the curse!

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:33.580
Keiichi-<i>san </i>suddenly started
screaming about being my Nii-Nii,

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:36.960
then grabbed the bat
from my brother's room.

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:41.510
The very same brother who went missing
due to the curse, Satoshi Hojo?!

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:43.840
I knew it! It's all connected!

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:45.890
I was right all along!

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:50.480
Keiichi-<i>san </i>attacked
my uncle with the bat...

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:55.860
But my uncle grabbed the bat
out of his hands and... and...

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:58.230
I tried to stop them,

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:04.660
but my uncle was just so angry
at Keiichi-<i>san </i>for getting CWS involved...

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:08.740
Nothing I said could get through to him.

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:13.250
But Keiichi-<i>san </i>didn't give up,
and he kept fighting my uncle...

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:18.250
I could have stopped them
if I'd tried harder...

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:22.720
Never mind that.
What else did Maebara-<i>san </i>say?

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:23.380
Huh?

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:24.260
The curse!

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:26.300
What did he say about the curse?!

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:33.850
That's right! When he was beating
my uncle, he kept saying something...

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:36.310
"This is Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>'s curse!"

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:41.530
Yes! I knew it!

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:45.410
The culprits were using our sweet,
obedient Maebara-<i>san </i>as their pawn!

00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:50.410
They must've asked him to carry out
the curse to prove his loyalty!

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:58.080
And this is the solid, undeniable proof!

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:01.000
Oyassan, after five long years,

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:05.800
I've finally found the connection
between Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>'s curse

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:08.140
and the string of murders in Hinamizawa!

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:13.390
Soon! Soon, I'll be able to come
to your grave and tell you the truth!

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:17.350
This proof will lead me straight to
the person behind the curse!

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:23.400
There are only a few people with the
authority to order something like this!

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:29.700
Think! <i>Think</i>, Kuraudo Ooishi!
There must be a clue somewhere!

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:31.580
I'm so happy for you.

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:35.410
So, Detective, how is your neck feeling?

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:36.710
My neck?

00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:40.210
Ugh, it's so itchy, so itchy!

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:43.800
Dammit, I was just about
to have the answer, too!

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:46.630
Why is it so goddamn itchy?!

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:50.760
My condolences. You must be
entering the final stage.

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:56.600
Who is it? Who gave the order?! Who?!

00:15:56.600 --> 00:16:00.730
Someone <i>ordered </i>this? Who would
tell someone to do something like this?

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:05.490
That's right! Keiichi-<i>san</i>
mentioned her name...

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:07.900
No!

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:09.570
She would never...

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:16.540
What did Maebara-<i>san </i>say?

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:20.000
Try to remember! What was it?!

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:25.130
He said that Rika told him to do this.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:27.090
Rika Furude!

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:30.510
She <i>is </i>the head of
one of the Three Families!

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:34.220
Of course the Furude Shrine
would carry out the curse!

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:37.930
I've connected all the pieces! This is it!

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:44.940
I finally have all the proof I need!

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:57.950
Now, go and shatter
Rika's heart into pieces,

00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:00.460
Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>'s dear familiar.

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:08.260
Doesn't look like Keiichi-<i>kun</i>
and Satoko-<i>chan </i>are back yet.

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:10.590
I'd better head home soon, too,

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:13.600
else old Gran will force me to
"make conversation" with my relatives.

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:15.970
Oh, I'll go with you.

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:18.890
I can stay the night in the guest house.

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:22.440
Why, if it isn't Miss Rika!
What's the matter?

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:27.940
Have you seen Tomitake?
You might have seen him with Takano.

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:31.780
Oh, yeah, I just saw them
in the parking lot...

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:36.330
Ooishi?

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.000
I've been looking for you,

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:43.420
Rika Furude-<i>san</i>!

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:46.750
Wha-- Detective?!

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.550
Are you drunk?!

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:52.680
Why?

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:56.220
Rika-<i>chan</i>!

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:58.100
What are you doing?!

00:17:58.100 --> 00:18:00.850
I finally solved the mystery!

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:02.890
Hey! Snap out of it--

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:26.330
You are such delightful
entertainment, children of man.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:27.380
Detective Ooishi!

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:30.260
I'll hear what you have to say!
I'm the next head of the Sonozaki Family!

00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:31.880
Just let go of Rika-<i>chan</i>!

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:33.510
What?

00:18:34.430 --> 00:18:35.590
No!

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:40.180
Mion! Now's your chance to get Rika--

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:42.390
Don't you get in my way!

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:43.440
Shion!

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:44.810
Stop...

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:55.950
My, it's getting quite lively.

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:59.700
No... way...

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:03.120
Please, stop.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:05.710
Shii-<i>chan</i>! Mii-<i>chan</i>!

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:08.790
Take care of Kei-<i>chan </i>for me, Rena.

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:15.760
<i>No!</i>

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:23.680
Rika-<i>chan</i>! Rika-<i>chan</i>!
Please, Ooishi-<i>san</i>, don't!

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:25.730
Now, confess! Tell me the truth!

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:28.860
You've already done so many
horrible things! You can take me instead!

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:28.860
Rika Furude!

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:37.660
How could this
perfect world end like this?

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:40.370
What? What'd you say?

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:42.700
Nothing. Just end it.

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:44.030
What?!

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:45.790
I won't reveal the secrets of the curse.

00:19:45.790 --> 00:19:48.040
You'll die knowing nothing.

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:50.130
You little brat!

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:55.590
Talk! Talk!

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:59.140
Talk! Talk!

00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:03.680
Talk! Talk! Talk!

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:06.940
Talk! Talk!

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:12.480
Talk! Talk! Talk!

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:16.320
Talk!

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:18.780
Satoko-<i>chan</i>! Stay back!

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:21.160
My, you're still not done?

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:25.080
For all your bark,
you're lacking in bite, Ooishi-<i>san</i>.

00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:26.120
Huh?

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:27.500
What?

00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:30.670
Is that how it is?!

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:33.090
<i>Now </i>I've got it!

00:20:33.090 --> 00:20:35.800
The <i>real </i>culprit manipulating
everything to their whim...

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:39.090
The person behind the curse
was <i>you </i>all along!

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:41.720
Yes, that's correct.

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:57.400
Rika? Are you quite dead?

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:05.990
If you're still alive, then I can't travel
to the next fragment with you.

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:10.580
Ah, yes, there's one way
to ensure you're dead.

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:16.760
Now I'm <i>certain </i>you're dead.

00:21:16.760 --> 00:21:19.340
S-Satoko-<i>chan</i>...?

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:22.180
Huh? What?

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:25.680
<i>No!</i>

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:29.850
I won't let you escape just yet, Rika.

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:33.520
Until you accept your happy future
with me in Hinamizawa...

00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:38.940
...I will never, ever let you
escape--and that's <i>for certain</i>.

00:21:55.670 --> 00:21:57.500
Now, then.

00:21:57.500 --> 00:22:00.300
Whatever will you do about this?

00:22:02.970 --> 00:22:07.930
Whatever <i>can </i>you do when you cannot even
view the fragments, O pitiful failure?

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:47.030
Kagurashi-hen:
God-Entertaining Chapter, Part 1

00:23:43.030 --> 00:23:46.860
Next time: "Kagurashi-hen:
God-Entertaining Chapter, Part 1."
